kanfei (0.1.0~beta23) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: wind gust is now the station's real gust.  On Davis Vantage
    stations the LOOP2 packet — which carries the console's own 10-minute
    gust, the 2- and 10-minute average wind, THSW index, and 15-minute and
    hourly rain — was requested incorrectly and never once arrived.  The
    console sent the first packet and stopped; the second read timed out
    and was discarded without a word, so the failure was invisible for the
    life of the install.  On the development station that was 714,779
    readings without a single LOOP2 value.  Because the published gust
    falls back to the largest wind reading since midnight when no real
    gust is available, dashboards, Weather Underground and CWOP/APRS have
    been receiving the daily maximum in place of a gust.  Expect your
    reported gust to change after upgrading — the console samples the
    anemometer far faster than the polling interval, so the old value
    systematically under-reported.  A missing LOOP2 packet is now logged
    rather than silently dropped.

  * Fix: an absent wind sensor no longer publishes a 255 mph gust.  When a
    Vantage transmitter drops out, the console reports the maximum byte
    value in the wind-speed field to mean "no reading".  That sentinel was
    stored as a real 255 mph measurement, and because the daily maximum
    outlives the outage that produced it, every subsequent upload carried
    the bad gust for the rest of the day — including to CWOP/APRS, where it
    was publicly visible long after the sensor recovered.  Sentinel values
    are now rejected on arrival, and the daily high/low figures are checked
    against each sensor's valid range before publication, a check that
    charts and CSV exports already applied but the published path did not.

  * Fix: sunrise and sunset times on Vantage stations.  Both were read from
    the wrong offsets in the LOOP packet, landing in the console's alarm
    block rather than the sun times, so the displayed values were unrelated
    to actual sunrise and sunset.  Transmitter battery status and console
    battery voltage are now read correctly as well, and a console reporting
    no clock is treated as unknown instead of midnight.

  * Adds full Davis Vantage command support, completing the driver: daily,
    monthly and yearly high/low retrieval; barometer calibration readout;
    EEPROM dump; receiver/transmitter status; clearing of stored highs and
    lows; setting yearly rain and evapotranspiration totals; full archive
    download; and setting station latitude and longitude over the wire.
    Several of these correct errors in Davis's own published documentation,
    each verified against real hardware; the discrepancies are catalogued in
    the repository for future reference.

  * Fix: station settings and clock controls are now offered based on what
    the connected station can actually do, rather than on its driver type.
    Vantage stations were shown controls that did nothing, and hidden from
    controls they supported.

