kanfei (0.1.0~beta21) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: the backup-restore endpoint now writes the restored database
    to the path your live install actually reads from, regardless of
    what the source backup's manifest called its database file.
    Previously, restoring a backup taken on an install whose database
    was named anything other than "kanfei.db" (notably the legacy
    "weather.db" naming used by Windows dev-checkout installs) would
    silently write to that source-named path instead of the live
    "kanfei.db", leaving the live install untouched and the user's
    data orphaned on disk — with a success message and no warning.
    This release derives the destination from KANFEI_DB_PATH directly
    and emits an INFO log line whenever the source and target
    filenames differ so the rename is visible.  The CLI restore
    command (python station.py restore) also picks up the same fix,
    including correct behaviour when restoring against a not-yet-
    existent destination on a fresh install.  Closes #179.

