kanfei (0.1.0~beta20) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: the 3D pressure-field view now renders with the intended smooth
    cubic-interpolated surface on every .deb install.  Since the 3D view
    first shipped, the backend's smooth-surface code path required scipy,
    but scipy was declared only in an optional "nexrad" dependency group
    that the .deb's postinst doesn't install — so every .deb-installed
    kanfei silently fell back to plain inverse-distance-weighting and the
    rendered surface was visibly bumpier than designed.  This release
    moves scipy into the main runtime dependencies; the postinst's
    existing pip-install step picks it up on first install or upgrade.
    Adds ~30MB to the venv install size.  Closes #177.

