kanfei (0.1.0~beta19) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: archive-period readings on legacy Davis stations (Weather Monitor /
    Wizard / Perception / GroWeather / Energy / Health) are correct for the
    first time.  A memory-map register declaration shipped at the wrong link
    bank since v0.1.0, so every read of the station's archive-period register
    returned a different garbage byte from an unrelated sensor field.  Effects
    observed by users: the history chart's time-bin resolution looked off
    because each archive row was tagged with a bogus interval; the
    station-config "archive period" value in Settings could show an impossible
    value like 68 or 102 minutes; and the daemon could push that bogus value
    back to the station's hardware register on every restart.  This release
    fixes the register address, validates every read and write against the
    Davis-legal set {1, 5, 10, 15, 30, 60, 120}, and ships a one-shot
    self-heal that runs on the first connect after upgrade: the daemon
    rewrites the canonical archive-period to the correct freshly-read value
    AND fixes every historical archive_records row that was tagged with a
    bogus interval — both in a single connect, no manual steps.  Vantage Pro
    and Vantage Pro 2 users are unaffected by this bug; they use a separate
    driver path that was never wrong.  Closes #174.

