kanfei (0.1.0~beta15) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: Davis barometer calibration field is no longer sign-inverted.
    The legacy BAR_CAL register stores its value with subtract-from-raw
    semantics (per reference/techref.txt:1070), but pre-fix kanfei
    exposed that raw register sign 1:1 through the UI, so a user who
    entered the intuitive "+456 thousandths inHg → add 0.456 inHg"
    actually got "−0.456 inHg" applied to their reading.  Negating at
    the kanfei-to-Davis I/O boundary makes the UI, the canonical
    station_config row, and apply_calibration all use the user-facing
    "add to reading" sign throughout; only the on-device register
    sees the negated form Davis expects.  A one-time
    bar_cal_sign_migration_v1 marker flips any existing pre-fix
    canonical row's barometer entry on first connect so working
    calibrations carry through the upgrade.  Scope: legacy LinkDriver
    only (Monitor II / Wizard III / Perception / GroWeather / Energy /
    Health) — Vantage and other drivers use different cal semantics
    and aren't affected.
  * Test infrastructure: tests/backend/conftest.py unconditionally
    overrides KANFEI_DB_PATH to a per-process temp file before any
    `app.*` import, so the suite can never touch the operator's real
    kanfei.db.  Closes a hazard that, post-#145/#148, would have wiped
    rows in sensor_readings, archive_records, users, and sessions for
    anyone who ran pytest in a shell with KANFEI_DB_PATH pointing at
    a populated database.
  * Routine dependency updates across the frontend: eslint v9 → v10
    (with @eslint/js and eslint-plugin-react-hooks bumped to match),
    react-router-dom 7.15.0 → 7.15.1, react-colorful 5.6.1 → 5.7.0,
    @react-three/fiber 9.6.0 → 9.6.1, @types/node 25.6.0 → 25.8.0,
    plus globals, react, and build-tools group bumps.  The eslint
    major bump introduced react-hooks 7.1.1 with a new
    react-hooks/set-state-in-effect rule that flags pre-existing
    patterns; CI does not run lint so the bumps land safely, with
    cleanup tracked separately.
  * Fix (UI re-roll): the Settings → WeatherLink section now gates
    every input/select and the Save button on a discrete load-status
    state until the live values land from the daemon.  Without the
    gate, the placeholder defaults (archive_period=30, sample_period=60,
    all-zero calibration) were displayed indistinguishably from real
    saved values during the serial-I/O latency window, and a user who
    typed corrections against those placeholders and hit Save could
    overwrite their actual settings.  The new load state distinguishes
    "still loading" from "load failed" (the latter happens when the
    logger daemon is down or the link isn't connected — the endpoint
    returns a 200 with an `{error: ...}` body) and surfaces the error
    with a retry link rather than silently locking the section forever.
    Also updates the Barometer Offset tooltip to reflect the post-cal-
    sign-fix semantics ("add to raw reading", with a pointer back to
    the sign-flip change).

 -- Chris Nighswonger <dev@veritassuperaitsolutions.com>  Mon, 18 May 2026 16:30:00 +0000

kanfei (0.1.0~beta14) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: archive backfill on reconnect now reaches the history chart.
